Zsh, Oh My Zsh, and configuration

Install:
  Install Zsh, Oh My Zsh, plugins and helper tools; back up and copy configuration; set the login shell to /bin/zsh.

Upgrade:
  Update or install Zsh, helper tools and external plugins; register the environment but preserve Zsh configuration and the login shell.

Status:
  Report package versions, plugin Git revisions, and configuration presence.

Requirements:
  Ubuntu, APT and a regular user with sudo access.

Configuration:
  Shell configuration: ${ZDOTDIR:-$HOME}/.zshrc and .zshenv
  A custom ZDOTDIR must also be configured in the shell startup environment.
  Oh My Zsh: ${ZSH:-$HOME/.oh-my-zsh}
  Custom configuration: ${ZSH_CUSTOM:-$ZSH/custom}/*.zsh (loaded by Oh My Zsh)
  Installation persists selected paths in .zshrc and ~/.config/wsley/zsh.sh.
  Open a new Zsh session after installation.
  The rm alias uses trash-cli; cleanup-dirs directly deletes matching caches.
  cleanup-dirs --include-generated also removes .venv, node_modules, and dist.
